        "original_id": "941b01ee-f476-51c5-925f-a0ac0fcf590e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Tropicana Products, PepsiCo, Pepsi-Cola Company, The Coca-Cola Company\n- People: Anthony T. Rossi\n- Products: Mountain Dew, Mello Yello\n- Places: Bradenton, Florida, United States, Canada\n- Topics: ownership, acquisitions, founding, competition\n\nFacts:\n- Anthony Talamo Rossi was born on September 13, 1900, and he died on January 24, 1993.\n- Anthony T. Rossi was an Italian immigrant who founded Tropicana Products in 1947 in Bradenton, Florida, in the United States.\n- Tropicana Products is a producer of orange juice.\n- In August 1964, the Pepsi-Cola Company acquired the Mountain Dew brand and production rights from Tip.\n- After the August 1964 acquisition, Mountain Dew distribution expanded more widely across the United States and Canada.\n- Mello Yello was introduced on March 1, 1979 by The Coca-Cola Company to compete with PepsiCo's Mountain Dew.\n- Since 1998, Tropicana Products has been owned by PepsiCo.\n- Tropicana Products grew from 50 employees to over 8,000 in 2004, expanded into multiple product lines, and became one of the world's largest producers and marketers of citrus juice.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
